# Debian/Ubuntu packages that need root or a system service. The apt
# equivalent of platform/fedora/packages, for the Linux server targets.
#
# This repository owns the user layer on a server and, through this file,
# the few root-level packages the environment itself needs. Hardening (ssh,
# firewall, unattended upgrades) is the server's own configuration, not here.
#
# How it is used:
#   platform/debian/bootstrap.sh  adds vendor repositories, then
#                                 `sudo apt-get install` on every name here
#   scripts/doctor                fails if a name here is not installed
#   scripts/inventory             prints this list
#
# Same rules as the Fedora file: one name per line, # comments; add here and
# `just sync`; remove here, then `sudo apt-get remove <name>` yourself.

# Tailscale. Needs the root daemon tailscaled, so a system package, from
# Tailscale's own apt repository, which bootstrap adds the way Tailscale's
# installer does. docs/tailscale.md.
tailscale
